; Strict-warning regression for the generated registration code: this
; (inline_tests) library compiles its modules with -w +a -warn-error +a,
; the harshest user regime, so every warning the PPX-generated code
; provokes is a build failure here. The fixture exercises let%test,
; module%test, and let%expect_test with every payload family (tagged,
; quoted, exact, bare, output) so each generated record shape — loc,
; payload, node — compiles with fully qualified fields: a field left to
; type-directed disambiguation is fatal warning 42 under these flags.
; The tests themselves pass; the regression is the build.

; Quiet-on-green, as in ../inline: the generated runner runs once per
; partition, and green partitions should not pay windtrap chrome.

(env
 (_
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_QUIET 1))))

(library
 (name windtrap_test_ppx_strict)
 (inline_tests)
 (flags
  (:standard -w +a -warn-error +a))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_windtrap)))
